# AbridgeAI frontend environment.
# Backend target: backend-new/abridgeai (no legacy backend supported).

# API base URL (override for staging/prod). Defaults to local dev.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1

# Route typed interview turns over the LiveKit data channel (topic `lk.chat`)
# instead of `POST /interview-sessions/{id}/respond`.
#
# Only "1" enables it (see lib/interview/text-transport.ts). Even when enabled,
# the LiveKit path needs THREE more conditions to be met — hybrid session,
# onboarding completed, room connected — and returns "rest" otherwise. So this
# flag widens what is possible, it does not force anything.
#
# Safe to leave on: every failure mode degrades to the REST path rather than
# breaking a turn. No worker, no LiveKit credentials, backend voice disabled
# (503 on the token mint), or a dropped room all resolve to "rest" and the
# candidate keeps interviewing.
#
# The trade-off to know about: that fallback is SILENT. Nothing in the UI
# distinguishes "carried over LiveKit" from "quietly fell back to REST", so
# do not treat a working interview as proof this flag did anything.
VITE_INTERVIEW_LK_TEXT=1
